# tools/hunk_artifact_witness.rish — an image proves itself content-addressed on metal (HUNK1).
#
# Season A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) · waymark HUNK · opening journey Open Image · rung HUNK1.
# Design read: active-designing/20260813-144218_hunk-season-a-open-image-exploration.md
# Teachers, thanked clean-room: gratitude/qoi.md (the open codec) · mantra/beading.rye (content-addressed store).
#
# HUNK0 proved decode(encode(pm)) recovers a pixmap byte-for-byte. This rung proves the next durable property:
# an image is a content-addressed Tablecloth artifact, so the store's own integrity guarantee becomes the
# image's. The module encodes a pixmap to QOI, beads it under a name (the name pins a SHA3 content address),
# and fetches by name — reassembly proving every bead against its digest FIRST, so a tampered bead refuses
# (DigestMismatch) before qoi.decode reads a single pixel. The selftest rides a real 8×8 image THROUGH the
# store byte-for-byte, shows the dedup dividend (the same image under two names stored once), and proves the
# tampered-bead and unknown-name refusals both land before any decode. No network, no key, no funds — the
# integrity seam beneath the parts marketplace and the Photos app.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/hunk_artifact_witness.rish

say "hunk-artifact: Language EN — HUNK1 gives a decoded image an identity: an image is a content-addressed Tablecloth artifact, so a name pins its bytes and a tampered bead refuses before a pixel is read."
say "hunk-artifact: Style Radiant — the store's content address becomes the image's integrity guarantee for free; the same image under two names is stored once, the dedup dividend the sprite-sheet marketplace will lean on."
say "hunk-artifact: Lens TAME — u32 in-memory counts, wire is bytes; every buffer names a maximum (max_stream_bytes bounds the fetch buffer to a resin); each function states its invariants positively; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "pond/bin/image_artifact"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p pond/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build pond/apps/image_artifact.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hunk-artifact: build failed — ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hunk-artifact: selftest exited non-zero — ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "hunk-artifact: ${out}"

assert out contains "GREEN image-artifact" else "hunk-artifact: selftest did not print the GREEN content-addressed line"

assert out contains "round-tripped THROUGH the content-addressed store byte-for-byte" else "hunk-artifact: round-trip through the store was not byte-for-byte"

assert out contains "before a pixel was read" else "hunk-artifact: the tampered/unknown refusals did not land before decode"

say "hunk-artifact: GREEN — an image is content-addressed; a name pins its bytes, a tampered bead refuses before a pixel is read."
